GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 83.3(7.2)(b) the adjournment is within 48 hours` MEANS
    IF NOT `the person is not released under paragraph (a)`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if the person is not released under paragraph (a), the adjournment may not exceed 48 hours"
    ELSE IF `the adjournment, in hours` AT MOST 48
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the adjournment may not exceed 48 hours"

§§ `83.3(8) to (14) the hearing, the recognizance and its conditions`

-- (8.1) "if the judge is also satisfied that the person was convicted previously of a terrorism offence, the judge may order that the person enter into the recognizance for a period of not more than two years" (GATE-A).
-- COVERS: fork F-ccc3-20 | s 83.3(8.1) the judge may order the recognizance for a longer period | s 83.3(8.1)
-- src:1841 | Duration extended
-- src:1842 | (8.1) However, if the judge is also satisfied that the person was convicted previously of a terrorism offence, the judge may order that the person enter into the recognizance for a period of not more than two years.
@ref s 83.3(8.1) (src:1841-1842)
GIVEN `the judge is also satisfied that the person was convicted previously of an offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offence is a terrorism offence, by s 2 terrorism offence` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 83.3(8.1) the judge may order the recognizance for a longer period` MEANS
    IF `the judge is also satisfied that the person was convicted previously of an offence`
    THEN CONSIDER `the offence is a terrorism offence, by s 2 terrorism offence`
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if the judge is also satisfied that the person was convicted previously of a terrorism offence"
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the offence is a terrorism offence is for s 2
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if the judge is also satisfied that the person was convicted previously of a terrorism offence"

-- (8)(a) GATE-A: "may, if the judge is satisfied by the evidence adduced that the peace officer has reasonable grounds for the suspicion, order that the person enter into a recognizance, with or without sureties,
-- to keep the peace and be of good behaviour for a period of not more than 12 months ..."; the period is `Length of time` (the core's type), compared by calendar months.
-- The third input is the FACT that is the gate of (8.1), not the answer of `s 83.3(8.1)`: that function answers NOTHING when its own gate fails (the 2026-11-12 ruling on grants with an "if"), so passing its answer here
-- would turn the flat cap of "not more than 12 months" into NOTHING for every longer period. JUST TRUE yes, JUST FALSE no, NOTHING not settled (finding in NOTES.md, seams).
-- COVERS: fork F-ccc3-11,F-ccc3-20 | s 83.3(8)(a) the judge may order that the person enter into a recognizance | s 83.3(8); s 83.3(8)(a)
-- src:1837 | Hearing before judge
-- src:1838 | (8) The judge before whom the person appears in accordance with subsection (3)
-- src:1839 | (a) may, if the judge is satisfied by the evidence adduced that the peace officer has reasonable grounds for the suspicion, order that the person enter into a recognizance, with or without sureties, to keep the peace and be of good behaviour for a period of not more than 12 months and to comply with any other reasonable conditions prescribed in the recognizance, including the conditions set out in subsections (10), (11.1) and (11.2), that the judge considers desirable for preventing the carrying out of a terrorist activity; and
-- src:1840 | (b) if the person was not released under subparagraph (7)(b)(i) or paragraph (7.1)(a) or (7.2)(a), shall order that the person be released, subject to the recognizance, if any, ordered under paragraph (a).
@ref s 83.3(8) (src:1837-1840)
GIVEN `the judge is satisfied by the evidence adduced that the peace officer has reasonable grounds for the suspicion` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the period of the recognizance` IS A `Length of time`
      `the judge is satisfied that the person was convicted previously of a terrorism offence, the gate of s 83.3(8.1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 83.3(8)(a) the judge may order that the person enter into a recognizance` MEANS
    IF NOT `the judge is satisfied by the evidence adduced that the peace officer has reasonable grounds for the suspicion`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may, if the judge is satisfied by the evidence adduced that the peace officer has reasonable grounds for the suspicion, order that the person enter into a recognizance"
    ELSE IF `the period is at most` 12
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE CONSIDER `the judge is satisfied that the person was convicted previously of a terrorism offence, the gate of s 83.3(8.1)`
              WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
                  IF `the period is at most` 24
                  THEN JUST TRUE
                  ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "for a period of not more than two years"
              WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "for a period of not more than 12 months"
              WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the judge is satisfied of a previous conviction of a terrorism offence is for subsection (8.1)
    WHERE
        `the period is at most` months MEANS
            (((`the period of the recognizance`'s years TIMES 12) PLUS `the period of the recognizance`'s months) LESS THAN months)
            OR (((`the period of the recognizance`'s years TIMES 12) PLUS `the period of the recognizance`'s months) EQUALS months AND `the period of the recognizance`'s days EQUALS 0)

-- (8)(b) "if the person was not released under subparagraph (7)(b)(i) or paragraph (7.1)(a) or (7.2)(a), shall order that the person be released, subject to the recognizance, if any, ordered under paragraph (a)".
-- COVERS: fork F-ccc3-6 | s 83.3(8)(b) the judge must order that the person be released, subject to the recognizance | s 83.3(8)(b)
@ref s 83.3(8)(b) (src:1837-1840)
GIVEN `the person was not released under subparagraph (7)(b)(i) or paragraph (7.1)(a) or (7.2)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 83.3(8)(b) the judge must order that the person be released, subject to the recognizance` MEANS
    IF `the person was not released under subparagraph (7)(b)(i) or paragraph (7.1)(a) or (7.2)(a)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the person was not released under subparagraph (7)(b)(i) or paragraph (7.1)(a) or (7.2)(a)"

-- (9) GATE-A: "may commit the person to prison for a term not exceeding 12 months if the person fails or refuses to enter into the recognizance".
-- COVERS: fork F-ccc3-11,F-ccc3-20 | s 83.3(9) the judge may commit the person to prison | s 83.3(9)
-- src:1843 | Refusal to enter into recognizance
-- src:1844 | (9) The judge may commit the person to prison for a term not exceeding 12 months if the person fails or refuses to enter into the recognizance.
@ref s 83.3(9) (src:1843-1844)
GIVEN `the person fails or refuses to enter into the recognizance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the term of imprisonment, in months` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 83.3(9) the judge may commit the person to prison` MEANS
    IF NOT `the person fails or refuses to enter into the recognizance`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if the person fails or refuses to enter into the recognizance"
    ELSE IF `the term of imprisonment, in months` AT MOST 12
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "for a term not exceeding 12 months"

-- (10) the firearms condition: the judge "shall consider whether it is desirable ... to include as a condition ... that the person be prohibited from possessing any firearm, cross-bow, prohibited weapon, restricted weapon, prohibited device,
-- firearm part, ammunition, prohibited ammunition or explosive substance, or all of those things ... and if the judge decides that it is so desirable, they shall add the condition". The nine things are named; the terms are those of section 2.1 (subsection 84(1)) and section 2.
-- COVERS: fork F-ccc3-6 | s 83.3(10) the judge must consider whether the condition is desirable; s 83.3(10) the judge must add the condition to the recognizance; s 83.3(10) the condition may prohibit the thing | s 83.3(10)
-- src:1845 | Conditions — firearms
-- src:1846 | (10) Before making an order under paragraph (8)(a), the judge shall consider whether it is desirable, in the interests of the safety of the person or of any other person, to include as a condition of the recognizance that the person be prohibited from possessing any firearm, cross-bow, prohibited weapon, restricted weapon, prohibited device, firearm part, ammunition, prohibited ammunition or explosive substance, or all of those things, for any period specified in the recognizance, and if the judge decides that it is so desirable, they shall add the condition to the recognizance.
@ref s 83.3(10) (src:1845-1846)
GIVEN `the judge is about to make an order under paragraph (8)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 83.3(10) the judge must consider whether the condition is desirable` MEANS
    IF `the judge is about to make an order under paragraph (8)(a)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Before making an order under paragraph (8)(a), the judge shall consider whether it is desirable"

@ref s 83.3(10) (src:1845-1846)
GIVEN `the judge decides that it is desirable, in the interests of the safety of the person or of any other person, to include the condition` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 83.3(10) the judge must add the condition to the recognizance` MEANS
    IF `the judge decides that it is desirable, in the interests of the safety of the person or of any other person, to include the condition`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the judge decides that it is so desirable, they shall add the condition to the recognizance"

@ref s 83.3(10) (src:1845-1846)
DECLARE `s 83.3(10) thing` IS ONE OF
    `s 83.3(10) a firearm`
    `s 83.3(10) a cross-bow`
    `s 83.3(10) a prohibited weapon`
    `s 83.3(10) a restricted weapon`
    `s 83.3(10) a prohibited device`
    `s 83.3(10) a firearm part`
    `s 83.3(10) ammunition`
    `s 83.3(10) prohibited ammunition`
    `s 83.3(10) an explosive substance`
    `s 83.3(10) something that is none of those`

@ref s 83.3(10) (src:1845-1846)
GIVEN thing IS A `s 83.3(10) thing`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 83.3(10) the condition may prohibit the thing` MEANS
    CONSIDER thing
    WHEN `s 83.3(10) something that is none of those` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "possessing any firearm, cross-bow, prohibited weapon, restricted weapon, prohibited device, firearm part, ammunition, prohibited ammunition or explosive substance, or all of those things"
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- COVERS: fork F-ccc3-6 | s 83.3(11) the judge must specify the manner and method | s 83.3(11)*
-- src:1847 | Surrender, etc.
-- src:1848 | (11) If the judge adds the condition described in subsection (10) to a recognizance, they shall specify in it the manner and method by which
-- src:1849 | (a) the things referred to in that subsection that are in the person’s possession shall be surrendered, disposed of, detained, stored or dealt with; and
