§ `Sections 83.31 to 83.33 -- Annual reports, sunset, transitional provision`

-- 83.31(2), (3), (3.1), (4): the annual reports on the operation of section 83.3. The AG of Canada and the Minister of Public Safety and Emergency Preparedness report to Parliament, the AGs and ministers of the provinces publish;
-- the content is a list ("that includes"), so an item not named is not covered; (4) bars information whose disclosure would do one of four things.
-- COVERS: encoded | s 83.31(2) the report must be prepared and laid before Parliament or published; s 83.31(2) the report includes the item | s 83.31(2)*
-- src:1863 | Annual report (section 83.3)
-- src:1864 | (2) The Attorney General of Canada shall prepare and cause to be laid before Parliament and the Attorney General of every province shall publish or otherwise make available to the public an annual report for the previous year on the operation of section 83.3 that includes
-- src:1865 | (a) the number of consents to lay an information that were sought, and the number that were obtained, by virtue of subsections 83.3(1) and (2);
-- src:1866 | (b) the number of cases in which a summons or a warrant of arrest was issued for the purposes of subsection 83.3(3);
-- src:1867 | (c) the number of cases in which a person was not released under subsection 83.3(7), (7.1) or (7.2) pending a hearing;
-- src:1868 | (d) the number of cases in which an order to enter into a recognizance was made under paragraph 83.3(8)(a), and the types of conditions that were imposed;
-- src:1869 | (e) the number of times that a person failed or refused to enter into a recognizance, and the term of imprisonment imposed under subsection 83.3(9) in each case; and
-- src:1870 | (f) the number of cases in which the conditions fixed in a recognizance were varied under subsection 83.3(13).
@ref s 83.31(2) (src:1863-1870)
DECLARE `s 83.31(2) item` IS ONE OF
    `s 83.31(2)(a) the number of consents to lay an information that were sought, and the number that were obtained, by virtue of subsections 83.3(1) and (2)`
    `s 83.31(2)(b) the number of cases in which a summons or a warrant of arrest was issued for the purposes of subsection 83.3(3)`
    `s 83.31(2)(c) the number of cases in which a person was not released under subsection 83.3(7), (7.1) or (7.2) pending a hearing`
    `s 83.31(2)(d) the number of cases in which an order to enter into a recognizance was made under paragraph 83.3(8)(a), and the types of conditions that were imposed`
    `s 83.31(2)(e) the number of times that a person failed or refused to enter into a recognizance, and the term of imprisonment imposed under subsection 83.3(9) in each case`
    `s 83.31(2)(f) the number of cases in which the conditions fixed in a recognizance were varied under subsection 83.3(13)`
    `s 83.31(2) another item`

@ref s 83.31(2) (src:1863-1870)
GIVEN `the report is for the previous year on the operation of section 83.3` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 83.31(2) the report must be prepared and laid before Parliament or published` MEANS
    IF `the report is for the previous year on the operation of section 83.3`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an annual report for the previous year on the operation of section 83.3"

@ref s 83.31(2) (src:1863-1870)
