    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "shall not contain any information the disclosure of which would"

-- 83.32(1) "Section 83.3 ceases to have effect at the end of the fifth anniversary of the day on which the National Security Act, 2017 receives royal assent unless, before the end of that fifth anniversary, the operation of that section is extended by resolution".
-- (2) the extension "may not exceed five years from the first day on which the resolution has been passed by both Houses"; (4) subsequent extensions read "on the expiry of the most recent extension under this section unless, before that extension expires".
-- The day of royal assent is not in the text (an input). Section 83.3 has effect through the fifth anniversary (or, if extended, through the last day of the most recent extension).
-- COVERS: fork F-ccc3-17 | s 83.32(1) section 83.3 has ceased to have effect on the day | s 83.32(1)
-- src:1885 | Sunset provision
-- src:1886 | 83.32 (1) Section 83.3 ceases to have effect at the end of the fifth anniversary of the day on which the National Security Act, 2017 receives royal assent unless, before the end of that fifth anniversary, the operation of that section is extended by resolution — whose text is established under subsection (2) — passed by both Houses of Parliament in accordance with the rules set out in subsection (3).
@ref s 83.32(1) (src:1885-1886)
GIVEN `the day on which the National Security Act, 2017 received royal assent` IS A DATE
      `the last day of the most recent extension by resolution passed by both Houses before the end of the period then running, if there is one` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day in question` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 83.32(1) section 83.3 has ceased to have effect on the day` MEANS
    IF `the day in question` GREATER THAN `the last day of effect`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "ceases to have effect at the end of the fifth anniversary of the day on which the National Security Act, 2017 receives royal assent unless"
    WHERE
        `the fifth anniversary` MEANS `add years` `the day on which the National Security Act, 2017 received royal assent` 5
        `the last day of effect` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the last day of the most recent extension by resolution passed by both Houses before the end of the period then running, if there is one`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN `the fifth anniversary`
            WHEN JUST extended THEN (IF extended GREATER THAN `the fifth anniversary` THEN extended ELSE `the fifth anniversary`)

-- (1.1) "A comprehensive review of section 83.3 and its operation shall be undertaken by any committee of the Senate, of the House of Commons or of both Houses of Parliament that may be designated or established ... for that purpose."
-- (1.2) "The committee shall, no later than one year before the fifth anniversary referred to subsection (1), submit a report on the review to the appropriate House of Parliament, or to both Houses, as the case may be,
-- including its recommendation with respect to extending the operation of section 83.3." Subsection (4)(b) re-reads "the fifth anniversary" as "the expiry of the most recent extension under this section" for a further extension.
-- These provisions bind a committee of Parliament and mean nothing to a person directly; they are encoded for what they decide (who must review, by when, with what in the report), with the dates as inputs.
-- COVERS: encoded | s 83.32(1.1) the committee must undertake a comprehensive review of section 83.3 and its operation | s 83.32(1.1)
-- src:1887 | Review
-- src:1888 | (1.1) A comprehensive review of section 83.3 and its operation shall be undertaken by any committee of the Senate, of the House of Commons or of both Houses of Parliament that may be designated or established by the Senate or the House of Commons, or by both Houses of Parliament, as the case may be, for that purpose.
@ref s 83.32(1.1) (src:1887-1888)
GIVEN `the committee is designated or established by the Senate or the House of Commons, or by both Houses of Parliament, for that purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 83.32(1.1) the committee must undertake a comprehensive review of section 83.3 and its operation` MEANS
    IF `the committee is designated or established by the Senate or the House of Commons, or by both Houses of Parliament, for that purpose`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "by any committee of the Senate, of the House of Commons or of both Houses of Parliament that may be designated or established"

-- COVERS: encoded | s 83.32(1.2) the last day for the committee's report | s 83.32(1.2); s 83.32(4)(b)
-- src:1889 | Report
-- src:1890 | (1.2) The committee shall, no later than one year before the fifth anniversary referred to subsection (1), submit a report on the review to the appropriate House of Parliament, or to both Houses, as the case may be, including its recommendation with respect to extending the operation of section 83.3.
-- src:1898 | (b) the reference to “the fifth anniversary referred to subsection (1)” in subsection (1.2) is to be read as a reference to “the expiry of the most recent extension under this section”.
@ref s 83.32(1.2) (src:1889-1898)
@ref s 83.32(4)(b) (src:1898)
GIVEN `the day on which the National Security Act, 2017 received royal assent` IS A DATE
      `the last day of the most recent extension by resolution passed by both Houses, if there is one` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 83.32(1.2) the last day for the committee's report` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the last day of the most recent extension by resolution passed by both Houses, if there is one`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `add years` (`add years` `the day on which the National Security Act, 2017 received royal assent` 5) (0 MINUS 1)
    WHEN JUST extended THEN `add years` extended (0 MINUS 1)

-- COVERS: encoded | s 83.32(1.2) the report is submitted in time | s 83.32(1.2)
@ref s 83.32(1.2) (src:1889-1890)
GIVEN `the last day for the report` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the committee submits the report` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 83.32(1.2) the report is submitted in time` MEANS
    IF `the day on which the committee submits the report` AT MOST `the last day for the report`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "no later than one year before the fifth anniversary"

-- COVERS: encoded | s 83.32(1.2) the report includes the committee's recommendation | s 83.32(1.2)
@ref s 83.32(1.2) (src:1889-1890)
GIVEN `the report includes the committee's recommendation with respect to extending the operation of section 83.3` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 83.32(1.2) the report includes the committee's recommendation` MEANS
    IF `the report includes the committee's recommendation with respect to extending the operation of section 83.3`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "including its recommendation with respect to extending the operation of section 83.3"

-- (2) the extension "may not exceed five years from the first day on which the resolution has been passed by both Houses".
-- COVERS: encoded | s 83.32(2) the extension is not more than five years | s 83.32(2)
-- src:1891 | Order in council
-- src:1892 | (2) The Governor in Council may, by order, establish the text of a resolution that provides for the extension of the operation of section 83.3 and that specifies the period of the extension, which may not exceed five years from the first day on which the resolution has been passed by both Houses of Parliament.
