-- 83.33(2) "In the event that section 83.3 ceases to have effect ..., a person detained in custody under section 83.3 shall be released when that section ceases to have effect, except that subsections 83.3(7) to (14) continue to apply
-- to a person who was taken before a judge under subsection 83.3(6) before section 83.3 ceased to have effect."
-- COVERS: fork F-ccc3-6,F-ccc3-15 | s 83.33(2) the person must be released when section 83.3 ceases to have effect; s 83.33(2) the provision continues to apply | s 83.33(2)
-- src:1900 | 83.33 (1) [Repealed, 2019, c. 13, s. 149]
-- src:1901 | Transitional provision — section 83.3
-- src:1902 | (2) In the event that section 83.3 ceases to have effect in accordance with section 83.32, a person detained in custody under section 83.3 shall be released when that section ceases to have effect, except that subsections 83.3(7) to (14) continue to apply to a person who was taken before a judge under subsection 83.3(6) before section 83.3 ceased to have effect.
@ref s 83.33(2) (src:1900-1902)
GIVEN `section 83.3 has ceased to have effect in accordance with section 83.32` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person is detained in custody under section 83.3` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person was taken before a judge under subsection 83.3(6) before section 83.3 ceased to have effect` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 83.33(2) the person must be released when section 83.3 ceases to have effect` MEANS
    IF NOT `the person is detained in custody under section 83.3`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a person detained in custody under section 83.3 shall be released"
    ELSE CONSIDER `section 83.3 has ceased to have effect in accordance with section 83.32`
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In the event that section 83.3 ceases to have effect in accordance with section 83.32"
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether section 83.3 has ceased to have effect is for s 83.32
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
             IF `the person was taken before a judge under subsection 83.3(6) before section 83.3 ceased to have effect`
             THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "except that subsections 83.3(7) to (14) continue to apply to a person who was taken before a judge under subsection 83.3(6) before section 83.3 ceased to have effect"
             ELSE JUST TRUE

@ref s 83.33(2) (src:1900-1902)
GIVEN provision IS A `Provision of the Code`
      `the person was taken before a judge under subsection 83.3(6) before section 83.3 ceased to have effect` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 83.33(2) the provision continues to apply` MEANS
    IF NOT `the person was taken before a judge under subsection 83.3(6) before section 83.3 ceased to have effect`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "to a person who was taken before a judge under subsection 83.3(6) before section 83.3 ceased to have effect"
    ELSE IF     provision's `section` EQUALS 83.3
            AND (    provision's `subsection` EQUALS "(7)" OR provision's `subsection` EQUALS "(7.1)" OR provision's `subsection` EQUALS "(7.2)"
                  OR provision's `subsection` EQUALS "(8)" OR provision's `subsection` EQUALS "(8.1)" OR provision's `subsection` EQUALS "(9)"
                  OR provision's `subsection` EQUALS "(10)" OR provision's `subsection` EQUALS "(11)" OR provision's `subsection` EQUALS "(11.1)"
                  OR provision's `subsection` EQUALS "(11.2)" OR provision's `subsection` EQUALS "(12)" OR provision's `subsection` EQUALS "(13)" OR provision's `subsection` EQUALS "(14)")
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "except that subsections 83.3(7) to (14) continue to apply"
